From 596b3af961fc7c3e7bf59e44a1ce4cadad0b8294 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The gVisor Authors <gvisor-dev@googlegroups.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:46:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: add tests of image, image view, and buffer view create
 info

The Vulkan specification makes the application responsible for valid
usage, and vkr gives the create info of the guest to the host driver
as it is. A driver on top of Metal turns that create info into Metal
descriptors. Metal does a validation of each descriptor in every
process and stops the process when a descriptor is not valid. The
guest is not trusted, so one guest command must not stop the renderer.

Add vkr_validate.c with tests of the valid usage rules that control
the content of those descriptors. vkr does the tests before it calls
the driver:

- Image create info (vkCreateImage and the three vkGetDeviceImage*
  commands): type, extent, mip level count, layer count, sample count,
  create flags, and the even extent of 4:2:0 and 4:2:2 formats. Then
  the image creation limits that the driver gives through
  vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2.
- vkCreateImageView: view type, level range, layer range, aspects,
  plane, component swizzle, format, slices, and usage. vkr_image keeps
  the create info of the image and the planes that have memory.
- vkCreateBuffer and vkGetDeviceBufferMemoryRequirements: size.
- vkCreateBufferView: range, format, element count, usage, and offset
  alignment. vkr_buffer keeps the size and the usage of the buffer and
  records that it has memory.
- vkBindImageMemory, vkBindBufferMemory, the image memory requirement
  commands, and the image subresource layout commands: the image, the
  buffer, the memory, the plane, and the subresource.

vkr_format_table.h gives the compatibility class, the texel block
size, and the plane formats of each format. A script of gvx
(scripts/gpu/gen_vkr_format_table.py) writes it from vk.xml of
venus-protocol.

A command with a result returns VK_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILED. A command
without a result stops the context. Each refusal writes one warning,
up to a fixed number of lines.

Also add a workaround for KosmicKrisp (Mesa 26.3). For a 3D image
with VK_IMAGE_CREATE_2D_ARRAY_COMPATIBLE_BIT or
VK_IMAGE_CREATE_2D_VIEW_COMPATIBLE_BIT_EXT, the driver makes a second
Metal texture of type 2D array with the mip level count of the 3D
image. A valid 3D image can have more levels than a 2D texture of its
width and height (1x1x8 with 4 levels), and Metal then stops the
process in vkBindImageMemory. ANGLE sets the flag on each 3D texture,
so the WebGL conformance page
conformance2/textures/misc/tex-storage-and-subimage-3d.html stopped
the renderer. For such an image, vkr removes the two flags and then
refuses 2D views of that image.
